WEBVTT

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.900
We’ve always been together

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.320
through hard times, painful times, and fun times.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.200
Supporting and helping each other, we’ve always fought together.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.770
She’d get mad at me if I
said she was my friend and that I love her,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.710
but to me, she’s my precious partner with whom I’ll walk the road to our dreams.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:30.100
To stumble, to regret, and to carry failure together.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.760
So let’s face it together.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.510
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.310
I guess that wraps up my report.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.140
The investigation unit will take care of the scene,
but everyone should cooperate with them as well.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.830
We’ll be on standby for a while.
If nothing happens, we’ll head back.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.820
Yes, ma’am!

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.650
As for Teana,

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.820
would you like to go for a stroll with me?

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.290
Yes, ma’am.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.210
Looks like you’ve messed up.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.920
I’m sorry.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.170
One shot went astray.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:19.660
I wasn’t at the scene,
but Lt. Vita has already scolded you,

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.290
so I think you’ve already reflected on your mistake.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.760
I won’t scold you a second time.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.490
But Teana, you try too hard every now and then.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.570
It’s becoming a bit of a problem.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.180
But you know, Teana,

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.770
you have to remember that you aren’t fighting alone.

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:45.420
Teana, our position in team combat has us surrounded by allies.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.510
That’s why you made your mistake today.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.290
Think about it carefully,
and make sure it doesn’t happen again.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.970
Can you promise me you’ll do that?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:55.290
Yes, ma’am.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.630
In that case, I’ll leave it at that.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.240
You’ve promised me, right?

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.100
Yes, ma’am.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.790
Understood, then...

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.980
Tia!

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.150
Subaru.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.320
I’m sorry for everything.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.660
Forget it.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.750
Were you scolded by Nanoha?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.750
A little bit.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.980
I see.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.500
Tia, it’s all right if you want to take a break over there.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.030
I’ll help with the investigation.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.930
After such a big mistake, I don’t want to be slacking off.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.260
Let’s do it together.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.100
Sure!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.870
Hey... Shari?

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:58.810
What’s up?

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:05.240
Is that person Fate’s with Dr. Yuuno, the archaeologist?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.820
That’s right, Dr. Yuuno Scrya.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:12.200
He manages the Time-Space Administrative Bureau’s database as the Infinity Library’s Chief Librarian.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:16.870
He is also an accomplished archaeologist,
excavating and performing research on ancient ruins.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:22.050
A Bureau operative and a civilian scholar would be the best way to describe him.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.390
He’s supposedly a childhood friend of Nanoha and Fate.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.660
I see, so the Jewel Seeds were...

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:36.720
Yeah. They were lent to a facility
along the coast from the Bureau’s warehouse.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.800
It seems they were stolen from there.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.150
I see.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.230
Well, we’re investigating their whereabouts.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:50.520
If I work with Riot Force 6 to pursue them,
we should be able to retrieve them.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.250
Fate, the person you’re after, Scaglietti...

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.140
But.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:03.590
When I saw the Jewel Seed, it really took me back.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.320
Even though there was a sad goodbye,

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.790
for me,

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:12.390
it was when my life truly began.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.480
Yuuno, Fate!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.190
Nanoha!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.900
Nanoha, perfect timing!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:24.820
I was asked to escort Dr. Yuuno
until Inspector Acous returns.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.710
Can I ask you to switch with me?

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.490
Roger.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.380
Erio, Caro, can you come help me observe the scene?

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:33.220
Yes, ma’am!

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.120
I’m coming.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.330
Well then, I’ll see you later.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.080
Right

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.310
Was today a coincidence?

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:55.430
It seems Inspector Acous knew that
Riot Force 6 would be on guard at the auction.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:07:00.610
And, well, he asked me to help
with the analysis of the objects being auctioned.

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:02.430
Is that so?

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.880
It seems your unit is doing well.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.530
Yep! It’s thanks to your sister Carim’s protection, Inspector Acous.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.480
It’d be great if I could do anything to help, but...

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:19.330
You’re always late or slacking off
but pretty busy generally, Inspector Acous.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.430
That’s mean!

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:28.200
Carim’s worried, too, about her cute little Rossa.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.080
I’m just as worried as she is!

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.630
Hayate, you’re like a little sister to Carim and me.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:40.380
Come to think of it, Rossa, are you friends with Yuuno?

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:47.380
When I went to search the Infinity Library one time, he personally showed me around.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:48.730
It was quite recently.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:54.780
Right! To all of Riot Force 6’s front-line troops,

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.730
withdrawal preparations are complete.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.200
Please assemble!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.750
Roger!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.410
Good work, everyone.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.060
You can have the afternoon off, okay?

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:10.010
Have something to eat, take a bath, and relax for tomorrow, okay?

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:10.860
Yes, ma’am!

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.300
Subaru,

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:20.000
I’m going to go practice on my own for a while.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.160
Self-training? I’ll come with you!

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.690
Then I’ll come too.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:24.730
Me too!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.690
You were told to take it easy, weren’t you?

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.110
You two go relax.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:34.280
And Subaru, sorry, but I want to train by myself.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:37.320
Fine...

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.790
You two, could I have a minute?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.240
Uh, I guess.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.700
Something’s been bothering me a bit during training.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:50.870
Concerning Teana.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:56.460
I know that all young mages want to get stronger,

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:59.210
and they’re usually a bit reckless,

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:01.720
but occasionally, she’s more than just reckless.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:05.390
Did something happen to her before she came here?

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:21.410
Tia has an older brother?

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.200
His ambition was to become an Enforcer. However,

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.660
since their parents both died in an accident,

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:33.510
Tia’s brother raised her by himself.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.150
But one day, on a mission...

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.910
Did he pass away?

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:43.930
Tia was only ten at the time.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.850
Teana’s brother, Tiida Lanster,

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.800
a captain in rank,

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:55.480
was part of the Air Armed Service and passed at the age of 21.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.520
He was rather elite, wasn’t he?

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:02.240
That’s right, he was an elite. That’s why,

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.150
during the mission where Captain Tiida died,

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:10.490
he managed to injure a wanted mage but

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.670
wasn’t able to catch him.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:16.790
Anyway, I heard that thanks to a lot of cooperation
from the Ground Armed Service,

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:20.920
he was captured on the same day, but...

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:26.630
After the incident, some heartless superiors made some pretty cruel comments.

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.440
It became quite a problem.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.610
Comments such as?

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:36.660
About letting the criminal
get away while he was chasing him.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:40.820
Saying he wasn’t worthy of being
an A.A.S. mage, as it was an unacceptable failure.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:45.290
That he wasted his life by failing to catch the criminal.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:52.460
Or to be more blunt, saying he was useless for failing the mission. Stuff like that.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.260
Teana was ten at the time.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:58.550
To lose her only relative,

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.710
and to have him deemed worthless and useless

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:03.260
during his final mission,

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:08.340
must have shattered her and broken her heart.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.110
That’s why Tia wants to prove

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.600
that the magic her brother taught her isn’t useless.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.090
That no matter the place,
no matter the mission, she can handle it.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.910
And to realize the dream he left behind,

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:29.280
the dream her brother couldn’t realize before he passed,

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.830
the dream to become an Enforcer.

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:39.930
That’s the reason Tia desperately tries so hard.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.850
You’ve been at it for four hours already.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:11:59.800
You’re going to collapse at this rate.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.780
Sergeant Vice.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.100
You were watching?

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:07.780
While I was performing maintenance on the helicopter,
I saw something glittering in the scope.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:12.200
I understand how you’re vexed that you missed that shot,
but sharpshooting isn’t something

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:14.960
you can become good at with a bit of practice swinging your gun around.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.580
It’d also be bad if you develop
bad habits through forced practice.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:23.960
But hey!

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:26.800
Isn’t that what Nanoha was telling you about a while ago?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:31.110
Nanoha, Siggy, the others, and I all go way back.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:38.290
Even so, if I don’t practice constantly, I won’t improve.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.720
I’m just an average person.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:44.100
An average person, huh?

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:48.360
From my perspective, you’re more than good enough.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.580
So much so that I’m jealous.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.000
Well, I don’t want to get in your way,

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.130
but for people like you,
your physical condition is everything.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.960
Take care of yourself, okay?

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.440
Thank you, sir.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.720
I’ll be fine.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:17.710
Tia!

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.880
What, you’re still awake?

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:25.860
I’ll be getting up at 0400 hours tomorrow.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.830
Sorry if my alarm’s noisy.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:31.040
That’s fine, but are you okay?

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:57.680
Tia?

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.610
Tia!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.710
Wake up, it’s 0400!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:04.780
Wakey-wake!

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.160
Sorry.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.480
I’m up.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.660
Are you going to practice?

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.850
I am.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.250
Right! Then, here are your training clothes.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.000
Thanks.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.290
Okay then, me too.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.670
Bu—why are you coming too?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:27.160
You can do more types of training with two people.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.080
I’ll come along!

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.040
It’s okay. I’m fine as it is.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:34.100
If you come with me, you won’t get enough sleep you know.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.520
You should know already.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.470
If it’s just our usual routine, I’ll be fine even if I don’t sleep for four or five days.

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:41.520
This isn’t like every day, though.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:45.480
Your training is especially intense. Make sure you get enough sleep.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:46.910
Don’t wanna!

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.530
Because we’re a team, Tia.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.990
Let’s do our best together!

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.430
Do what you want!

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.420
So, what’s this thing you were thinking about, Tia?

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:06.550
For the time being, there’s a way to quickly improve our combat abilities.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:11.470
If we can do it well, our combination attacks will be more versatile and cover a greater area.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.250
Erio and Caro will be able to follow us better, too.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.640
That sounds exciting.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.330
Right? First...

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.560
Well then, let’s keep focusing on individual skills, okay?

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:28.160
It might seem like we’re just doing the basics over and over, but you all need to keep at it!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:28.800
Yes, ma’am!

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:34.990
Teana, Subaru, you two look in a good mood somehow.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.940
Did something happen?

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.050
N-No.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:39.970
Nothing.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.580
Teana! Be more agile!

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:51.880
Subaru, perhaps it should move more like this.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:56.530
I won’t be able to proceed
when that doesn’t work.

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:05.850
My main skill will still be
sharpshooting. First, last and always.

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.940
It’s the precision shooting
that my brother taught me,

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.040
but if that’s all I can do, then...

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.520
I have to keep improving
my combat skills and movement.

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:02.920
Sorry for making you do so much work, Cross Mirage.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:05.060
No problem.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:11.540
After tomorrow’s mock battle is over, I’ll ask Shari to give you a full tune-up.

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:12.530
Thank you.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:15.760
I’m back!

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.190
Tia, here.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:19.430
Thanks.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.300
I wonder if tomorrow’s mock battle

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:24.800
will go well.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:28.650
If it goes well, the success rate is pretty borderline, I guess.

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:32.020
If it’s that much, I’m sure it’ll be fine!

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:37.360
But are you sure you’re okay with it?

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.120
With what?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:43.330
In a way, we’ll be going against

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:46.370
your hero, Nanoha.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.290
I’m used to being scolded and making other people mad.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:53.960
Even if it means going against her,
we’re doing this to become stronger!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.150
If we fight properly, I’m sure she’ll understand.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:01.100
Because Nanoha’s a nice person.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:08.690
Well then, tomorrow’s early morning
special training is our last rehearsal, so go to sleep quickly.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:18.700
Well then, to conclude the morning, we’ll have some 2-on-1 mock battles.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.240
First will be Stars.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.400
Get your Barrier Jackets ready.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.160
Yes, ma’am!

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.930
Erio and Caro will be observing with me.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:27.450
Yes, ma’am!

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.400
Let’s do it, Subaru!

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.570
Right!

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.930
The mock battle’s started already!

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:40.250
Fate!

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.370
I thought I was supposed to be helping, though.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.170
It’s Stars’s turn now.

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:48.610
I was going to be in Stars’s mock battle.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:53.180
Ah. Nanoha really tries too hard while training sometimes.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:55.060
If she doesn’t get some rest...

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:59.780
Even when Nanoha goes back to our room, she’s always looking at the monitors.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:05.120
Making the training plans,
checking everyone’s formations on video...

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.330
Nanoha.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:11.540
All through training, she’s always watching out for us.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.940
She really is. Always.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.300
Hey, she’s using Cross Shift.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.320
<b>Crossfire Shoot</b>

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.330
Somehow, it doesn’t look very refined.

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.750
Her control looks good, but...

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.710
No, even if that was it...

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.960
That’s not a fake! It’s really her?

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:59.350
Come on, Subaru!

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:02.470
Dangerous maneuvers like that are poor form!

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:08.350
Sorry! But I’ll properly defend for it.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.310
Where’s Teana?

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.910
A bombardment attack? From Teana?

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:23.170
The results of our special training: Cross Shift C

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.110
Let’s go, Subaru!

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:48.680
Tia!

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.020
The Tia over there is an illusion?

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:54.510
Then where’s the real one?

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:02.510
I’ll pierce her barrier and then break through her field.

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:04.530
It’ll take her out in one hit!

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:10.320
Raising Heart.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.820
Mode release.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:12.560
All right.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.090
Nanoha!

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.020
It’s strange.

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:28.680
You two, what’s gotten into you?

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:38.480
I know you’re trying your best,
but a mock battle isn’t a brawl.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:42.140
If you’re just pretending to listen during practice

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:46.320
and then acting so recklessly during the real thing,

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:49.280
then training has no meaning, does it?

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:53.560
Let’s do it properly, like we do in practice.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.240
Okay?

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:00.210
What I’m asking is,

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:02.510
is my training

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.860
really that bad?

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.030
Blade erase.

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:15.640
I just don’t want anyone to get hurt anymore!

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.510
I don’t want to lose anyone anymore!

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:18.480
Tia.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:22.190
That’s why I want to get stronger!

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:27.360
Why don’t you cool your head a bit?

00:22:29.190 --> 00:22:30.640
Crossfire...

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:34.040
<b>Phantom Bla—</b>

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:35.500
...Shoot

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:40.190
Tia!

00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:41.370
A bind?

00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:44.110
Stay still and watch.

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:50.610
Nanoha!

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:05.780
Tia!

00:23:08.730 --> 00:23:10.910
The mock battle ends here.

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:14.120
Today, the two of you have been shot down.

00:25:17.620 --> 00:25:19.370
The things
we want to convey.

00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:21.520
The meaning of courage.

00:25:21.520 --> 00:25:24.370
Most importantly, the things we should protect.

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:35.350
Till the day each can fly on their own.
